.TH UNIM 1 "July 2026" "UNIM 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim \- Universal Next-generation Input Method for Korean
.SH DESCRIPTION
UNIM is a Korean Input Method Engine (IME) written in Rust with a 3-layer
architecture: Core Engine \(-> DBus Daemon \(-> Frontend IM Modules.
.PP
It supports GTK3/4, Qt5/6, XIM (X Input Method), Wayland, and GNOME Shell,
providing hangul composition, hanja conversion, special character input,
TypeFix (typo correction), smart backspace, and emoji search.
.PP
Since 0.3.0, hanja/special-character/emoji popups are rendered by a
dedicated sidecar process \fBunim-popup-service\fR(1) via the
\fBorg.atit.unim.Popup\fR D\-Bus interface. On GNOME Wayland the GNOME Shell
extension renders popups directly using St widgets.
.SH COMPONENTS
.TP
.B unim-daemon
The D\-Bus daemon that runs the input engine. Communicates with frontends
via \fBorg.atit.unim.InputMethod\fR on the session bus.
.TP
.B unim-popup-service
Popup rendering sidecar. Subscribes to \fBorg.atit.unim.Popup\fR and renders
GTK4 popup windows for hanja, special-character, and emoji candidates.
Started automatically via D\-Bus session activation.
.TP
.B unim-cli
Unified command-line tool for text conversion (eng\(<->kor) and settings
management (via the \fBconfig\fR subcommand).
.TP
.B unim-gui-gtk
System tray indicator and settings dialog (GTK4/libadwaita).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored in \fB~/.config/unim/config.yaml\fR.
.PP
Key settings:
.TP
.B engine.default_category
Default input mode: Korean or English (default: English)
.TP
.B engine.mode_sharing
Mode sharing: Global or PerApp (default: Global)
.TP
.B engine.korean.layout
Korean layout profile name: ko_2bulstd, ko_3bul390, ko_3bul391,
ko_3bul_noshift, ko_3bul_anmatae, or any user profile in
~/.config/unim/layouts/
.TP
.B engine.korean.chord_window_ms
Moachigi chord window duration in milliseconds. 0 = disabled.
Valid range: 10\(en200 ms. Default: unset (disabled).
.TP
.B engine.korean.bidirectional_combine
When true, jamo combinations are tried in both (a,b) and (b,a) order.
Default: unset (disabled).
.TP
.B engine.english.layout
English layout: qwerty, dvorak, colemak, colemak_dh, workman
.TP
.B engine.toggle_keys
Han/Eng toggle keys (default: Korean, RightAlt)
.TP
.B engine.hanja_keys
Hanja/special char keys (default: Hanja, F9). Idle press opens emoji popup.
.TP
.B engine.app_rules
Per-app default mode rules (JSON array of {app_pattern, default_category})
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B TypeFix (AutoTypeFix)
Auto-detect and convert mistyped text between Korean and English.
Forward: English typed in Korean mode. Reverse: Korean typed in English mode.
Triggered by double-tap of the toggle key (inline) or Super+K (selection).
A learning blacklist suppresses repeated false corrections.
.TP
.B Moachigi (chord input)
Chord-based simultaneous jamo input for supported layouts (e.g.
ko_3bul_anmatae). Multiple jamo pressed within chord_window_ms are combined
into a single syllable using Atomic Window Principle.
.TP
.B Smart Backspace
Decompose committed hangul syllables by jamo unit when backspacing.
.TP
.B Content Type Detection
Automatically blocks hangul mode in password/PIN input fields.
.TP
.B Emoji Search
Keyword-based emoji popup via Hanja key when no composition is active.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
User configuration file
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/layouts/*.json
User keyboard layout profiles (v1 schema)
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/typefix-blacklist.yaml
AutoTypeFix suppression dictionary (auto-managed)
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/userdict.yaml
User dictionary for reverse AutoTypeFix
.TP
.B ~/.unim-errors.log
Debug log (active when UNIM_DEVELOP=1)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UNIM_DEVELOP
Set to "1" to enable debug logging across all components.
